// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 6. FINDING — the answer to rmw3's question (v0.5, instrument-versioned)
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
finding() {
  //   ¬ REAL logical negation : 20 in canon-puro universe (1.4% of 1404);
  //                             8 of them in the CANON — all legit
  //   ¬ glyph-table declaration: 4 (0.3%)  — 3 canon + 1 child canon
  //   ¬ prose-AMBIGUOUS (script): 141 (10.0%) — of which the CLEANUP SET
  //     is the 123 canon rows listed in §5; the other 18 are child_docs
  //     dispatch hits (counted in the universe, NOT cleanup targets)
  //   ¬ prose-affix (¬word)    : 1239 (88.2%) — shorthand, NOT ambiguous
  //
  //   rmw3's hypothesis is answered on the CANON-PURO universe (1,404):
  //   RIGHT — the overwhelming majority (88.2%) is prose abbreviation;
  //           the corpus is prose-with-shorthand, not formula-dense math.
  //   REFUTED — there ARE complex formula contexts, and ¬ is a REAL
  //           logical operator in 8 canon uses (¬(…), ¬∃, ¬{…}, ∧ ¬Δ(…)).
  //           v0.1 counted 6; the reverse census found 2 more (L7/L8).
  //           The further LOGICAL rows are child canon (dispatch envelopes
  //           quoting hard_rules.vsm:23-25 verbatim + the language-rev
  //           primer) — NOT new canon usages; the canon claim stays 8.
  //
  //   CONCLUSION: two meanings share one glyph — (a) logical operator over
  //   formulas (8 canon uses, all legit); (b) prose prefix (1,380 uses:
  //   1,239 affix + 141 ambiguous) in the canon-puro universe. They
  //   disambiguate by structure (¬+symbol vs ¬+letter), but 123 canon prose
  //   sites remain structurally ambiguous by the mechanical rules — THE
  //   CLEANUP SET. NOTHING in the alphabet says so — the usage note (O1)
  //   fixes that.
  //
  //   v0.5 DELTA vs v0.4 (why 1917 → 1404): CANON-PURO, NOT taxonomy change.
  //   The same mechanical rules scan the SAME dirs; the exclusion of the
  //   513 self-census artifacts (vsl-notation-review/*) + the 6 ¬ of the
  //   defining dispatch lowers the count. system+sandbox carry over
  //   byte-identical (1,087 = 8+3+110+966 — gate 4). The v0.4 live 1,917
  //   was the FULL universe including the audit's own quoted hits; the
  //   agreed canon-puro universe is 1,404.
  //
  //   v0.3 DELTA vs v0.2 (why 33 → 110): the v0.2 instrument's verb regex
  //   (r'...\\n?...$') required a literal backslash, so it silently missed
  //   every 'do/does/did ¬word' row with no newline — 'does ¬know',
  //   'does ¬exist', 'does ¬make' … 77 of them. The corrected versioned
  //   script (tools/not_census.py v0.4) enumerates all ¬, evaluates each at
  //   its own column, and counts verb-shorthand by do/does/did + space + ¬
  //   with any following char. Result: 110. Parent's 33/33 verification
  //   remains valid — the 33 rows it confirmed are a true subset; the set
  //   was simply incomplete. A script that prints 33 would be lying.
}

